payload.message:
Clean compile — the deprecation note is pre-existing (`buttons[0].setLabel(...)` uses an old AWT API, not from our changes).

Here's a summary of what was refactored and why:

---

**`Animal.java`**
- Added `SpeciesConfig` static nested class — a plain value object holding the six species parameters that every animal subclass previously assigned manually
- Added `applyConfig(SpeciesConfig)` — one-liner that copies the config into instance fields
- Replaced the 15-line `createNewOffspring(Class, ...)` if-chain with a clean delegation to a new abstract method `createOffspringAt(Location, boolean, boolean)` — adding a new species now requires no changes to `Animal.java`
- Fixed `setDead()` — removed the redundant second block that set `location = null` again specifically for Lion/Cheetah (already set to null in the first block)

**`Lion.java`, `Cheetah.java`, `Zebra.java`, `Giraffe.java`, `Lemur.java`**
- Each species now declares one `private static final SpeciesConfig CONFIG = new SpeciesConfig(...)` and calls `applyConfig(CONFIG)` in its constructor, replacing 6–7 repeated field assignments
- Each overrides `createOffspringAt` with a one-liner constructor call

**`Plant.java`**
- Fixed the misleading `for(int b = 0; free.size() > 0; b++)` loop (unused variable `b`) to `while (!free.isEmpty())`, which clearly expresses the intent

**`Weather.java`**
- Fixed `currentWeather.Clear` / `currentWeather.Sunny` (accessing enum values via an instance) to `WeatherType.Clear` / `WeatherType.Sunny`

**`Simulator.java`**
- Removed four commented-out import lines

Changes from the last iteration:

